{"step_index":2893,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-29T07:33:20Z","thinking":"**Analyzing Merkle Catch Design**\n\nI'm now diving into the Vector-Merkle DAG \"Merkle Catch\" architecture. I'm focusing on Anthony's suggestion to integrate this design into both the \"brains\" and \"containers.\" My current focus is on evaluating the benefits of this architectural shift. I'm considering how this might extend functionality.\n\n\n**Designing Semantic Merkle Catch**\n\nI'm now focusing on the 18,432-dimensional vector integration within the Merkle DAG, as the vectors offer commitment to meaning, not just bytes. This shift enables semantic embedding for each node in the DAG. The node structure I am considering consists of the node ID, parent hash, timestamp, agent ID, raw text, the vector, Poincaré norm, and the Merkle root. I'm checking existing scripts for health checks, catch logging, and building a preflight health gate with stage checks and local model verification.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"write_to_file","args":{"CodeContent":"#!/usr/bin/env python3\n\"\"\"\nXORAS PRE-DELIBERATION HEALTH GATE & VECTOR-MERKLE DAG AUDITOR\n100% AIR-GAPPED & OFF-GRID BARE-METAL BINDING LAW\n\nVerifies:\n1. Port 8080 Sovereign Stage HTTP Response (200 OK)\n2. Local Models (gemma4:26b, llama3.2:3b, sovereign-jarvis, qwen2.5-coder):\n   - Checksum / Digest validation against manifest\n   - Model load & HTTP socket connectivity\n   - Probe prompt payload verification (live inference response)\n3. Cryptographic Merkle DAG & 18,432-D Vector Embedding signed receipts appended to CATCH_LOG.md\n4. Auto-Routing Lock: Flag dark nodes & update identity/active_routing.json\n\"\"\"\n\nimport sys\nimport os\nimport json\nimport time\nimport hashlib\nimport urllib.request\nimport urllib.error\nfrom datetime import datetime, timezone\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\nROOT = Path(__file__).resolve().parent.parent.parent\nMANIFEST_FILE = ROOT / \"identity\" 